== tool -h
! Loads a property file and dumps it to stdout, optionally converting between encodings.
! Escape sequence handling can also be disabled (it is enabled by default).
! 
! Usage:
!  jproperties [-h] input_file [input_encoding [output_encoding [process_escapes]]]
! 
! The input and output encodings default to `utf-8'. If `false' is given for the
! `process_escapes' parameter, then escape sequences in property values are taken
! literally, i. e. they are treated like normal characters. This will also cause
! the writer to try hard not to output any escape sequences in values and thus it
! will output everything literally, as long as this does not lead to invalid output.
exit 1
== tool
! Loads a property file and dumps it to stdout, optionally converting between encodings.
! Escape sequence handling can also be disabled (it is enabled by default).
! 
! Usage:
!  jproperties [-h] input_file [input_encoding [output_encoding [process_escapes]]]
! 
! The input and output encodings default to `utf-8'. If `false' is given for the
! `process_escapes' parameter, then escape sequences in property values are taken
! literally, i. e. they are treated like normal characters. This will also cause
! the writer to try hard not to output any escape sequences in values and thus it
! will output everything literally, as long as this does not lead to invalid output.
exit 1
